                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was looking forward to this game, but shortly after starting it I realized, it is not for me :(\n\nIt's hard to read, I just wish all of those many characters would stop their babbling. And this is a bad thing, because it is a VN. I just couldn't get into it. I don't like the \"humor\", but this is just my taste. \nWhat really annoyed me was the \"Japanese setting\", while none of this feels Japanese in the slightest. More like Euopeans fantasize and imagine about Japanese culture and life -_-\nSo it would have been much more convincing if the developers just set up their story in a European country. It might be a lot better this way, maybe to the point of slightly enjoyable. Oh well. I'll force myself to play the game though, just in case. \n\nOh, and one thing. This game has no skip function (just like their other game, Final Theosis, where every path except one dialoge is exactly the same... and was still better than Pawn), so this is a real no-go for me. Minizes the replay value, most people don't want to read the same stuff more than once just to get other endings.",
